## This repository is an aggregation, not a single work

The AGPL-3.0 grant in `LICENSE` covers **the application source code** authored
for this project — the Elixir under `lib`, the JavaScript and CSS under
`assets`, the tests, and the configuration.

It does **not** relicense the third-party material bundled alongside it. Those
files keep their own terms, and anyone redistributing this repository is bound by
those terms in addition to the AGPL. The practical consequences are set out
below, because two of them restrict what you may do with the repository as a
whole.

## Bundled third-party material

### Map base artwork — CC BY-NC-SA 4.0

`priv/static/images/maps/*.svg` (10 files) are derivative works of the
[Escape from Tarkov SVG Maps Project](https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-dev-svg-maps)
by Shebuka, re3mr and contributors, licensed
[CC BY-NC-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/).

Full provenance, the list of modifications, and the upstream terms are in
[`priv/static/images/maps/ATTRIBUTION.md`](priv/static/images/maps/ATTRIBUTION.md).

Three terms carry over to you:

1. **ShareAlike** — adaptations of this artwork must stay under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
   and keep the credit above.
2. **NonCommercial** — this artwork may not be used commercially. It is why EFT
   Buddy carries no advertising, no paid tiers and no sponsorships. **A fork that
   monetises this project while shipping these files would breach the artwork
   licence, whatever the AGPL permits for the code.**
3. **No cheating use** — the upstream terms forbid use in software that confers
   an unfair in-game advantage (radar/ESP overlays, cheat-client maps,
   automation, pixel bots), and state that such use revokes the licence
   automatically. EFT Buddy renders these maps as static reference material: it
   does not read game memory, parse game logs, hook the client, or track live
   player position. **Any feature that changed that would void the licence and
   must not be built.**

### Map projection configuration — MIT

The per-map transform, bounds, zoom range, floor layers and room labels are
synced at runtime from the `maps.json` of
[tarkov.dev](https://github.com/the-hideout/tarkov-dev) and stored in this
application's database. MIT requires its notice to travel with copies, and that
data is copied into our database and served to clients, so the notice
(`Copyright (c) 2019 Oskar Risberg`) is reproduced in full in
[`priv/static/images/maps/ATTRIBUTION.md`](priv/static/images/maps/ATTRIBUTION.md).

### Typefaces — SIL Open Font License 1.1

`priv/static/fonts/*.woff2`: Oswald (Copyright 2016 The Oswald Project
Authors) and Inter (Copyright 2020 The Inter Project Authors). Full licence texts
ship beside the fonts as `OFL-Oswald.txt` and `OFL-Inter.txt`; see
[`priv/static/fonts/README.md`](priv/static/fonts/README.md). Neither
family declares a Reserved Font Name.

### Vendored JavaScript — MIT

`assets/vendor/topbar.js` — topbar 3.0.0, Copyright (c) 2024 Buu Nguyen, MIT
